Z||000000||Bautsch||08-12-99||06:40 AM||||I just got my first Fiero. It's an 88 coupe 4 cylinder. I really wanted to get a 6 but when I saw the condition of this car I had to get it and hope I could convert it to a 6. Does anybody have any experience with doing this type of conversion? There are plenty of parts cars available in my area that have good or rebuildable engines in them. Would I need an 88 to do this or would any year be suitable? I have many questions but if anybody has done this they probably already know what the questions are. Thanks for any help you can provide.<p>Mike Bautsch<br>mike@macvend.com
Z||000001||theogre||08-12-99||07:38 AM||||the v6's are pretty much all the same, but finding the right mounts for the 88 could be a pain. You can't just drop the cradle and stuff in the v6 from another year. the cradels don't interchange between 88 and previous years. If you could find a v6 88 then it would save you allot of work.<p>You'll need the whole parts car for this one. you need all the engine wire, the ECM, fuel pump, and half a hundred other assorted things. you'll want the tach too. It's not hard if you take your time, allot of time..... 
Z||000002||ChadMan||08-12-99||07:44 AM||||I think SCCAFIERO is doing exactly this - taking the V6 from an 86 SE and installing it in an 88 Coupe.  I'd scroll through here until you find one of his posts, then email him with questions.
